Create a 9:16 premium editorial campaign using a realistic portrait, floating transparent optical units, strong typography, and a believable product.

Give the optical elements real thickness, beveled edges, reflections, refraction, and clear three-dimensional depth. Arrange them with a deliberate visual rhythm rather than randomly.

Keep most of the face clear, with at least one unobstructed eye. Only distort areas actually covered by the transparent material, using subtle and physically believable optical effects.

Let the same optical behavior affect typography or products behind the material so the portrait, glass, text, and product feel like one photographic space.

Use an oversized headline, clear brand information, meaningful product copy, restrained colors, realistic skin and materials, and polished editorial composition.

Avoid duplicated facial features, random distortion, plastic skin, fake UI, barcodes, badges, filler text, and decorative clutter.

The final result should feel like a real high-end fashion, beauty, jewelry, eyewear, skincare, or luxury campaign with a clear Floating Optical Units concept.
